<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomField xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <CustomField> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
        matching parent xml file" error.

        DISPOSITION GAP CLOSURE TRANCHE 2, ITEM 5b (agent-output/disposition-gap-closure-t2-design.md
        §3 item 5b; Gate 1 decisions D-12/D-13/D-14, 2026-08-31). Captures the free-text reason a
        Principal gives when overriding the Sell Meter and starting a disposition on a YELLOW-band
        asset (stories 12/14). This REVERSES a recorded scope decision — lwc/sellMeterList's
        _confirmOverride header previously stated "there is still no override REASON field ... a
        deliberate scope decision, not an oversight." That paragraph is retracted in place, quoting
        it, by the developer agent building 5b's LWC/Apex half — not in this file.

        Shape (LongTextArea, length 4000, visibleLines 3) per the design doc's item 5b table.
        Not required at the platform level (see below for why "required" is enforced elsewhere) and
        no default value.

        =====================================================================================
        FLS (to be applied in the consolidated permission-set pass, NOT this file — owned by
        salesforce-solution-architect per design §4).
        =====================================================================================
        READ-ONLY FLS in BOTH DPEG_Disposition_View AND DPEG_Disposition_Edit (editable=false in
        both). This is a MACHINE-WRITTEN AUDIT FACT stamped by SYSTEM-mode Apex
        (DispositionService.initiateAndSubmit, step 4, at insert, only when the band is YELLOW) —
        not an analyst-editable judgement field. Precedent, quoted from
        objects/NDA__c/fields/Principal_Approved__c.field-meta.xml, itself citing
        BOV_Broker_Change__c's 2026-08-20 code-review reconciliation (C3): a similarly
        approval/audit-written field's allowEdit grant was refused "on the grounds that granting
        allowEdit would let the very analyst who replaced a broker go back and rewrite who did it
        and when." The same reasoning applies here: the analyst who triggers the override must not
        be able to rewrite the reason after the fact. A Metadata-API-deployed field carries NO FLS
        for anyone, System Administrator included, until that consolidated pass lands.

        WHY "REQUIRED" IS NOT SET ON THE FIELD ITSELF: per design D-14, mandatoriness on the
        override path is enforced client-side by c/sellMeterOverrideModal's confirm-disabled
        getter (the same idiom sellMeterInitiateModal.confirmDisabled already uses, because
        `required` on a lightning-* input only fires on reportValidity(), which nothing calls) and
        server-side by the fact that DispositionService only stamps this field on the override
        path at all. Making the FIELD itself platform-required would block every other DML against
        Disposition__c that does not go through the override path.

        RELATED: the paired audit signal, Sell_Decision_Trigger__c = 'Principal Decision', is
        stamped in the SAME DML — no new picklist value, no record-type surgery; that value
        already exists on both record types (design P-7). See DispositionService.cls's header for
        that stamp once the developer agent's pass lands.

        NOT a child/log object (contrast BOV_Broker_Change__c, which IS append-only because a
        broker can be replaced many times per disposition). The override happens AT MOST ONCE per
        Disposition__c — both create paths early-return on an existing disposition, and the meter
        governs starting a sale, never reopening one. Cardinality 1 ⇒ a field on the parent.

        Risk: LOW as schema. One new field, no picklist change, no record-type edit. The risk in
        this item lives entirely in the Apex/LWC half (developer agent) and the FLS grant
        (solution-architect agent), not here.
    -->
    <fullName>Sell_Meter_Override_Reason__c</fullName>
    <description>Machine-written audit fact: the Principal&apos;s free-text reason for overriding the Sell Meter and starting a disposition on a YELLOW-band asset. Stamped by DispositionService.initiateAndSubmit at insert, only on the override path. Read-only FLS in both disposition sets - see this file&apos;s XML comment.</description>
    <inlineHelpText>Reason given by the Principal for overriding the Sell Meter on a YELLOW-band asset. Machine-written at the time of override; not editable afterwards.</inlineHelpText>
    <label>Sell Meter Override Reason</label>
    <length>4000</length>
    <trackHistory>false</trackHistory>
    <trackTrending>false</trackTrending>
    <type>LongTextArea</type>
    <visibleLines>3</visibleLines>
</CustomField>
